---
description: MontroneDSP Git attribution and commit authorship policy
alwaysApply: true
---

Git commits created for MontroneDSP-owned work must use the owner's configured
Git author and committer identity.

Never append automatic AI-agent co-author trailers.

In particular, never append:

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

Do not add equivalent Cursor co-author or autogenerated attribution trailers.

Do not misattribute genuine human contributions. Preserve legitimate authorship
when working with commits originally authored by another person.

Before every commit, verify the final commit message and Git identity.

After every commit, inspect the actual stored commit object.

Before every push, inspect every outgoing commit for unwanted attribution.

If the editor or agent automatically adds a trailer, correct the responsible
setting or mechanism and reject the affected commit before publication.

Never rewrite main, force-push protected branches, or change repository
protection to correct attribution.

Never assume a correct git user.name automatically prevents co-author trailers.
